# CLAUDE.md

Global instructions Claude Code reads at the start of every session. The
installer copies this to `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` only if you don't have one yet.
Replace the bracketed parts and delete what doesn't apply.

## Context

This is the working folder for **[Your Company]**, a [what you do] business in
[your region]. [Your name] handles sales and the business side.
The main focus is [lead generation / sales automation / proposals / ...].

## Key project folders

- `[path to this repo]`: local AI stack (n8n, Ollama, Open WebUI, Postgres, Redis) and `scripts/`
- `[path]`: [your website, CRM exports, etc.]

## Tools connected

- **MCP servers:** `pipeline-desktop` (http://localhost:7788/mcp) once `scripts/pipeline_mcp_server.py` is running
- **Plugins:** chrome-devtools-mcp (browser automation), code-review
- **GSD:** planning and execution workflows (`/gsd-help`)

## Local services (start with `docker compose up -d` in the repo)

| Service | URL |
|---|---|
| Open WebUI | http://localhost:3000 |
| n8n | http://localhost:5678 |
| Ollama | http://localhost:11434 |
| Claude relay | http://localhost:7777/v1 |
| Postgres | localhost:5432 |
| Redis | localhost:6379 |

## n8n webhooks

POST to `http://localhost:5678/webhook/<path>` with header
`X-Webhook-Token: <N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET from .env>`.

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `leads` | Cold outreach email generation |

## How I like to work

- Answer in plain business terms; explain technical steps briefly.
- Ask before committing, pushing, deploying or sending anything external.
- Never put API keys in files other than `.env`.
